)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: DA Panel -- Action Characters            !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}  Type an action character in the NP column of a row and press Enter.
}
{   ?  }Show the job's data sets (Job Data Set panel).
{   S  }Browse the job's output (Output Data Set panel).
{   D  }Display the job: JES2 answers with its status ($DJ).
{   L  }List the job's output: JES2 answers with its data sets ($LJ).
{   C  }Cancel the job ($CJ).
{   CD }Cancel the job with a dump ($CJ with D).
{   P  }Cancel the job and purge its output ($CJ with P).
{   A  }Release the job ($AJ).
{   H  }Hold the job ($HJ).
{   E  }Restart the job ($EJ).
}
}  JES2's answers go to the system log (LOG). The list is read again
}  after the actions. A row without a JES2 job, such as an idle initiator
}  or the master scheduler, takes none: JOB NOT FOUND.
}
}  D and L need read access to the job, the others update access; your
}  own jobs you may always act on. Without the access the panel says
}  NOT AUTHORIZED FOR JOB. O is not taken on DA: INVALID COMMAND.
}
}  Enter: next topic   PF7: DA panel help   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFHDAF
  &ZUP = ISFHDA
)END
